# The robot assets under models/turtlebot3_*/ and the worlds under worlds/ are
# generated, but they are COMMITTED rather than ignored: rebuilding them needs
# an NVIDIA GPU, Isaac Sim and turtlebot3_description, which is too steep a
# bootstrap for someone who only wants to clone the package and launch it, and
# is not available in CI at all. They are 2 MB and change approximately never.
# scripts/build_models.sh is the way to regenerate them, not the way to obtain
# them. See README.md, "The robot asset and the worlds".

# Generated nav2 maps: built from a world by scripts/build_map.py. Still
# ignored -- the warehouse .pgm alone is 1.4 MB and is rebuilt whenever the
# slice, the bounds or the world changes.
maps/*.pgm
maps/*.yaml

# Python bytecode, written by the container (root) when the scripts run
__pycache__/

# Personal Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json
